45 701.0 Td (ALGORITHM 3: InsertionSort\(A[0..n-1]\)) Tj
45 689.0 Td (---------------------------------------) Tj
45 677.0 Td (// Sort by inserting each element into its correct sorted position.) Tj
45 665.0 Td () Tj
45 653.0 Td (  comparisons <- 0) Tj
45 641.0 Td (  FOR i <- 1 TO n-1 DO) Tj
45 629.0 Td (      key <- A[i]) Tj
45 617.0 Td (      j   <- i - 1) Tj
45 605.0 Td (      WHILE j >= 0 AND A[j] > key DO) Tj
45 593.0 Td (          comparisons <- comparisons + 1) Tj
45 581.0 Td (          A[j+1] <- A[j]) Tj
45 569.0 Td (          j <- j - 1) Tj
45 557.0 Td (      END WHILE) Tj
45 545.0 Td (      IF j >= 0 THEN comparisons <- comparisons + 1 END IF) Tj
45 533.0 Td (      A[j+1] <- key) Tj
45 521.0 Td (  END FOR) Tj
45 509.0 Td (  RETURN A, comparisons) Tj
45 497.0 Td () Tj
45 485.0 Td (Step-by-Step Logic:) Tj
45 473.0 Td (  1. Treat A[0] as a one-element sorted sub-array.) Tj
45 461.0 Td (  2. Pick next element \(key\); walk backwards through sorted portion.) Tj
45 449.0 Td (  3. Shift all elements greater than key one position right.) Tj
45 437.0 Td (  4. Insert key into the gap. Sorted portion grows by 1. Repeat.) Tj
45 425.0 Td () Tj
45 413.0 Td (Complexity: Best=O\(n\) [sorted] | Average=O\(n^2\) | Worst=O\(n^2\) [reversed]) Tj
45 401.0 Td (Characteristic: Most adaptive of the three ? excellent for nearly-sorted data.) Tj
45 389.0 Td () Tj
45 377.0 Td (COMPLEXITY TABLE:) Tj
45 365.0 Td (  Algorithm     | Best   | Average | Worst  | Stable | Adaptive) Tj
45 353.0 Td (  --------------+--------+---------+--------+--------+---------) Tj
45 341.0 Td (  Selection     | O\(n^2\) | O\(n^2\)  | O\(n^2\) | No     | No) Tj
45 329.0 Td (  Bubble        | O\(n\)   | O\(n^2\)  | O\(n^2\) | Yes    | Yes) Tj
45 317.0 Td (  Insertion     | O\(n\)   | O\(n^2\)  | O\(n^2\) | Yes    | Yes) Tj
45 305.0 Td () Tj
45 293.0 Td (MATHEMATICAL DERIVATION:) Tj
45 281.0 Td (  Selection Sort:  Comparisons = SUM\(i=0 to n-2\)\(n-1-i\) = n\(n-1\)/2) Tj
45 269.0 Td (  Bubble worst:    Comparisons = n\(n-1\)/2  \(same sum\)) Tj
45 257.0 Td (  Insertion worst: Comparisons = SUM\(i=1 to n-1\) i = n\(n-1\)/2) Tj
45 245.0 Td () Tj
45 233.0 Td (RECOMMENDATION: Use INSERTION SORT for the emergency dispatch system.) Tj
45 221.0 Td (  Reason: Emergency data is typically nearly-sorted \(incremental updates\).) Tj
45 209.0 Td (  Insertion Sort achieves O\(n\) for sorted/nearly-sorted; it is STABLE and) Tj
45 197.0 Td (  ADAPTIVE. Selection Sort is never adaptive ? always avoid for this context.) Tj
45 185.0 Td () Tj
